module

public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.AdicQuotientModuleSiteQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.AffineAdicTowerR1LimVanishing

/-!
# The affine adic-tower comparison at a pseudo-coherent object

`exists_isIso_comp_limit_sections_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isAffineOpen` of
`Completion/AffineAdicTowerR1LimVanishing.lean` carries three hypotheses: the derived-limit
presentation `hlim` of part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K], the quasi-coherence `hqc` of every
cohomology sheaf of every term of the adic reduction tower, and the Mittag-Leffler condition
`hML` one degree below. This file removes the middle one at the object part (2) of that tag is
stated for — a pseudo-coherent `K` — and keeps the general form untouched beside it.

## Main results

* `exists_isIso_comp_limit_sections_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isPseudoCoherent`
  — the same comparison `H^q(U, K^∧) ≅ lim_n Γ(U, H^q(K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹))` over an affine open,
  with `hqc` discharged.

## Why `hqc` costs nothing here

`hqc` is [Stacks, Tag 08DX] applied to the tensor factorization of each term of the tower, and
[Stacks, Tag 08DX] wants both factors to have quasi-coherent cohomology. The quotient factor
`𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹` has it on any locally Noetherian scheme at any `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isQuasicoherent_adicQuotientModule_idealSheafSiteSubmodule`), and the
factor `K` has it as soon as `K` is pseudo-coherent, by [Stacks, Tag 08E5]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isQuasicoherentDerived_of_isPseudoCoherent`). Both halves are already
assembled into
`Stacks.Algebraization.isQuasicoherent_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isPseudoCoherent` of
`Completion/AdicQuotientModuleSiteQuasicoherent.lean`, so all this file does is apply it.

## What is still open on the route to part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]

Both remaining hypotheses, and this corollary therefore does not close that part.

* `hlim` is part (1) of the same tag in de-existentialised form. It is proved for an ideal sheaf
  generated by a finite family of global sections,
  `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_adicReductionTower_generatedIdealSheaf`,
  but not at an arbitrary `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, which is what relating `ℐ`
  to a global generating family would take.
* `hML` carries the mathematical content of the vanishing and is proved only on the module side,
  as the first conjunct of [Stacks, Tag 0EGV]. Transporting it needs a projection formula
  exchanging derived sections with the derived tensor product, and no such comparison is in the
  library in any generality. The module documentation of
  `Completion/AffineAdicTowerR1LimVanishing.lean` records both gaps in full.

So the statement below is deliberately left carrying `hlim` and `hML`, and it is not registered
against [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]: discharging a side condition of a comparison is not the comparison.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08E5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08E5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.HypercohomologyEdge (derivedSections hypercohomologyEdge)
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (opensRingedSite)
open AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite (adicReductionTower derivedCompletion derivedCompletionAdicFactor)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

section AdicTowerPseudoCoherent

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (𝓘 : X.IdealSheafData)
  (K : DerivedCategory X.Modules)

-- the same instance the general form of the comparison was elaborated against, so that the
-- product in the type of `hlim` is the same one there and here
attribute [local instance 100000] hasProductsOfShape_nat_affineAdicTower

/-- **`H^q(U, K^∧) ≅ lim_n Γ(U, H^q(K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹))` over an affine open, for a
pseudo-coherent `K`.**
`exists_isIso_comp_limit_sections_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isAffineOpen` with its
quasi-coherence hypothesis `hqc` discharged by
`Stacks.Algebraization.isQuasicoherent_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isPseudoCoherent`:
pseudo-coherence of `K` gives quasi-coherent cohomology sheaves by [Stacks, Tag 08E5], the
quotients `𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹` have them on any locally Noetherian scheme, and [Stacks, Tag 08DX] combines
the two across the derived tensor product.

The remaining two hypotheses are unchanged, and both are genuinely open: `hlim` is part (1) of
[Stacks, Tag 0A0K] at an arbitrary quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals, and `hML` needs a projection
formula for derived sections that the library does not have. The general form of the comparison
is kept beside this one, since it applies at a `K` that is not pseudo-coherent. -/
public theorem exists_isIso_comp_limit_sections_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isPseudoCoherent
    (hK : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent (X := X.toRingedSpace) K)
    (V : X.affineOpens)
    (hlim : NoetherianAdicCompletion.IsDerivedLimitWithProjections
      (adicReductionTower (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K)
      ((derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K)
      (fun n : ℕ ↦ derivedCompletionAdicFactor (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
        (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K (n + 1)))
    (q : ℤ)
    (hML : IsMittagLefflerCategorical
      (adicReductionTower (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K ⋙
        DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor X.Modules (q - 1) ⋙
          _root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) (op V.1))) :
    ∃ c : (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, V.1)) q).obj
          ((derivedSections (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) V.1).obj
            ((derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K)) ⟶
        limit (adicReductionTower (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K ⋙
          DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor X.Modules q ⋙
            _root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) (op V.1)),
      IsIso c ∧ ∀ n : ℕ,
        c ≫ limit.π (adicReductionTower (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
              (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K ⋙
            DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor X.Modules q ⋙
              _root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) (op V.1))
            (op n) =
          (hypercohomologyEdge (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) V.1 q).app
              ((derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
                (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K) ≫
            (_root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace)
              (op V.1)).map ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor X.Modules q).map
                (derivedCompletionAdicFactor (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
                  (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) K (n + 1))) :=
  exists_isIso_comp_limit_sections_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isAffineOpen 𝓘 K V hlim
    (isQuasicoherent_homology_adicReductionTower_of_isPseudoCoherent 𝓘 K hK) q hML

end AdicTowerPseudoCoherent

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
